# ============================================================================
#  PUSHUP LEAGUE — ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ============================================================================
#
#  HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#  --------------------
#  1. Copy this file to a new file called  .env.local   (same folder)
#         Windows PowerShell:   Copy-Item .env.example .env.local
#         Mac / Linux:          cp .env.example .env.local
#  2. Fill in the values you need.
#  3. Restart the dev server (stop it with Ctrl+C, then `npm run dev` again).
#
#  GOOD NEWS: to run the app on your own computer you do NOT need to change
#  anything in this file. The defaults below use a local database file and
#  everything just works. You only need to fill things in when you deploy.
#
#  NEVER commit .env.local to GitHub. It is already listed in .gitignore.
#  Anything in this file is a secret unless it is marked "safe to share".
# ============================================================================


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  1. WHICH DATABASE TO USE
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  "sqlite"   = a single file on this computer. No account, no setup. Great for
#               developing and for running the app yourself.
#               THIS IS THE DEFAULT — you can leave this line commented out
#               while working locally.
#
#  "postgres" = a real database server. REQUIRED when you deploy to a host like
#               Vercel, because those hosts wipe the local disk on every deploy
#               and your users would lose all their push-ups.
#
# DB_DRIVER=sqlite


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  2. LOCAL DATABASE FILE  (only used when DB_DRIVER=sqlite)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Optional. Defaults to ./data/pushup-league.db inside the project folder.
#  Safe to share. You never need to set this.
#
# SQLITE_PATH=./data/pushup-league.db


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  3. PRODUCTION DATABASE  (only used when DB_DRIVER=postgres)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  >>> SECRET. Never share this. Never paste it into front-end code. <<<
#
#  Where to get it (Supabase — free):
#    1. Sign up at https://supabase.com
#    2. Click "New project". Pick a name, a database password, and the region
#       closest to you. Wait ~2 minutes for it to finish setting up.
#    3. Left sidebar -> Project Settings (the gear) -> Database
#    4. Find "Connection string" -> choose the tab "URI"
#    5. Copy it. It looks like:
#         postgresql://postgres.abcdefgh:YOUR-PASSWORD@aws-0-eu-west-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
#    6. Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the database password you chose in step 2.
#    7. Paste the finished string after DATABASE_URL= below.
#
#  Tip: the "Connection pooling" / port 6543 string is the right one for a
#  website. It handles many short-lived connections much better.
#
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.xxxx:your-password@aws-0-region.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  4. DATABASE ENCRYPTION
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Optional. Leave it alone for Supabase — encrypted connections are switched on
#  automatically whenever DATABASE_URL is not localhost.
#  Set to "disable" only if you run your own Postgres locally without SSL.
#
# DATABASE_SSL=disable


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  5. PASSKEY / FACE SIGN-IN DOMAIN
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Optional. Safe to share. You normally do NOT need to set these.
#
#  Passkeys are permanently tied to a web address: one created on
#  http://localhost:3000 will not work on https://pushupleague.com. The app
#  works this out from the incoming request, so localhost and your deployed
#  address both work with no configuration.
#
#  Set these only if your site is served through a different hostname than
#  users type (for example an apex domain redirecting to www).
#
# WEBAUTHN_RP_ID=pushupleague.com
# APP_ORIGIN=https://pushupleague.com


# ============================================================================
#  QUICK REFERENCE
# ============================================================================
#
#  Running locally on your own computer
#  ------------------------------------
#    Nothing to fill in. Just leave this file alone (or don't create it at all).
#
#  Deployed and shared with friends
#  --------------------------------
#    DB_DRIVER=postgres
#    DATABASE_URL=<your Supabase connection string>
#
#  Which values are secret?
#  ------------------------
#    DATABASE_URL          SECRET  — full access to every user's data
#    SQLITE_PATH           safe
#    DB_DRIVER             safe
#    WEBAUTHN_RP_ID        safe
#    APP_ORIGIN            safe
#
#  There are no API keys in this project. Push-up detection runs entirely in
#  the browser, so there is no computer-vision service to pay for or to leak.
# ============================================================================
